Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] phy: sun4i-usb: guard PHY_CTL_VBUSVLDEXT

Not all chips have PHY_CTL_VBUSVLDEXT. Pretending they always do may lead
to undefined behavior.

Add a configuration quirk and avoid setting the bit when it is enabled.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
@@ -188,6 +188,7 @@ struct sun4i_usb_phy_cfg {
 	bool phy0_dual_route;
 	bool needs_phy2_siddq;
 	bool siddq_in_base;
+	bool no_vbus_valid_ext;
 	bool poll_vbusen;
 	int missing_phys;
 };
@@ -449,7 +450,8 @@ static int sun4i_usb_phy_init(struct phy *_phy)
 	if (data->cfg->siddq_in_base) {
 		if (phy->index == 0) {
 			val = readl(data->base + data->cfg->phyctl_offset);
-			val |= PHY_CTL_VBUSVLDEXT;
+			if (!data->cfg->no_vbus_valid_ext)
+				val |= PHY_CTL_VBUSVLDEXT;
 			val &= ~PHY_CTL_SIDDQ;
 			writel(val, data->base + data->cfg->phyctl_offset);
 		}
-- 
